   "reasoning_summary": "C19H13NO2, DoU 14. No carbonyl carbon (highest 152.0) and no OCH/OCH3 protons, so oxygens are aromatic (furan-type) or nitro. Two aliphatic 1H signals (8: 2.83, 9: 2.65) fit aryl methyls; only one sp3 carbon (27: 20.0) observed, implying overlap. Then 6 H methyl + 7 ArH (1-7) = 13 H, requiring a C17H9NO2 fully aromatic core with DoU 14, satisfied by a pyridine fused to two benzofurans. Carbons 10-13 (142-152) are O/N-bearing aromatic carbons, 23-26 (106-117) shielded carbons ortho/beta to furan O, and the isolated pyridine CH next to N explains the 9.33 signal (1). A methyl-nitro benz[a]anthracene is an alternative fitting the formula but explains the shielded carbons and second methyl signal poorly. Methyl positions are tentative due to missing multiplicities/integrals."
  },
